@startuml oxebots_lifecycle_safety_architecture
title OxeBots Firmware Architecture - LifecycleSupervisor State Machine

left to right direction

!include style.iuml
!include implementation_priorities.iuml
!include health_types.iuml

state "LifecycleState::BOOT" as Boot
state "LifecycleState::SELF_TEST" as SelfTest
state "LifecycleState::DISARMED" as Disarmed
state "LifecycleState::ACTIVE" as Active
state "LifecycleState::DEGRADED" as Degraded
state "LifecycleState::SAFE_STOP" as SafeStop
state "LifecycleState::CALIBRATION" as Calibration

Boot : outputs forced safe
Boot : load identity + calibration

SelfTest : verify mandatory buses + actuators
SelfTest : classify optional sensor failures

Disarmed : PWM = 0
Disarmed : kick inhibited

Active : execute bounded motion command
Active : kick only through independent gate

Degraded : keep only capabilities marked safe
Degraded : report fault + fallback in telemetry

SafeStop : PWM = 0 before direction update
SafeStop : kick inhibited
SafeStop : latch reason in HealthState.latched_faults

Calibration : wheel encoders + IMU sensors
Calibration : wheel PID tuning
Calibration : command execution disabled

[*] -right-> Boot
Boot -right-> SelfTest : <back:#FFFFFF>platform initialized</back>
SelfTest -right-> Disarmed : <back:#FFFFFF>mandatory interfaces ready</back>
Disarmed -right-> Active : <back:#FFFFFF>fresh permitted command</back>
Active -right-> Degraded : <back:#FFFFFF>HealthState.severity = recoverable</back>

Active -down-> SafeStop : <back:#FFFFFF>command timeout</back>\n<back:#FFFFFF>or HealthState.severity = critical</back>
SafeStop -left-> Disarmed : <back:#FFFFFF>explicit clear + HealthState restored</back>
Disarmed -down-> Calibration : <back:#FFFFFF>calibration request</back>

note top of Active
  LifecycleSupervisor PRIORITY_P0

  LifecycleSupervisor command-authority order:
  1. electrical + actuator safety
  2. command freshness
  3. calibration-mode
  4. base-station motion + kick intent
end note

note right of SelfTest
  Mandatory initialization failure enters SAFE_STOP.
end note

note right of Degraded
  Recovery returns to ACTIVE.
  Explicit disable returns to DISARMED.
  A critical fault enters SAFE_STOP.

  Examples:
  - ToF unavailable: motion allowed, kick inhibited
  - rejected magnetometer: use vision/gyro heading
  - one wheel feedback source lost: use remaining estimate
  - telemetry TX failure: receive until timeout
end note

note bottom of Calibration
  Completion or cancellation returns to DISARMED.
  Any unsafe condition enters SAFE_STOP.

  Calibration routines include the accelerometer,
  gyroscope, magnetometer and wheel encoders.
end note

note right of SafeStop
  This transition is available from every mode for:
  - command timeout
  - unsafe supply voltage
  - motor stall or implausible wheel motion
  - loss of all feedback for any driven wheel
end note

legend bottom
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#DCFCE7> Green | Implemented and compatible boundary |
  |<#FEF3C7> Amber | Partially implemented |
  |<#DBEAFE> Blue | Target component |
  |<#FEE2E2> Red | Existing component to replace or adapt |
  |= Priority |= Implementation order |
  | P0 | Safety and drivable foundation |
  | P1 | Closed-loop motion and state estimation |
  | P2 | Local perception and game features |
  | P3 | Calibration and tuning support |
  | DONE | Compatible implementation already exists |
endlegend

@enduml
